WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.027
Auracle is a Rust workspace of five
crates, compiled to WebAssembly.

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:10.168
Here's how a patch becomes a sound,
and a choice becomes a model.

00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:15.779
A patch is a term in a typed grammar:
a probabilistic program over modules.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:21.249
Every knob and every structural choice has
a trace address, so a whole patch is one

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.359
draw from a prior.

00:00:23.057 --> 00:00:28.271
It compiles to a quiver signal graph,
which runs one sample at a time with no

00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:30.235
allocation on the audio path.

00:00:30.914 --> 00:00:36.167
Every candidate plays the same standard
phrase, normalized for loudness, through a

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.434
vetting gate that rejects
silence, clipping and DC.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.680
From that phrase come eighteen perceptual
features, from brightness and noisiness to

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.941
envelope shape and three
bands of modulation rate.

00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:52.464
Twenty-six structural ones
come from the patch itself.

00:00:52.464 --> 00:00:54.160
Every one is standardized.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.315
Taste is a utility: the maximum over a
few linear experts on those features.

00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:05.578
A duel, a keep or a cut, a star
rating: each has its own likelihood.

00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:11.574
The posterior is sampled by Markov chain
Monte Carlo, and each new answer reweights

00:01:11.574 --> 00:01:14.103
those samples until a refit is due.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.982
Every duel is forecast
before it's answered.

00:01:17.982 --> 00:01:22.978
Each forecast is scored with a proper
scoring rule, separately for each kind of

00:01:22.978 --> 00:01:23.978
evidence.

00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:29.977
Search targets a Boltzmann distribution:
the grammar's prior, tilted by expected

00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:30.977
utility.

00:01:30.876 --> 00:01:35.444
Refinement is Metropolis-Hastings
on the trace, through fugue-evo.

00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:37.451
A lock is exact conditioning.

00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:44.061
PERFORM's named controls are fixed directions
in that standardized space of sound.

00:01:44.411 --> 00:01:49.900
For each patch, a finite-difference Jacobian
and a ridge solve wire each control to

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:54.596
its knobs. Every half of every control
is then checked on real renders.

00:01:55.914 --> 00:02:01.392
In the browser, the engine runs in a
worker, and the voices in an AudioWorklet.

00:02:01.392 --> 00:02:04.582
A render farm measures
candidates in parallel.

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:09.659
Every claim here has a measurement
behind it, in the reference.

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:11.502
Read it, run it, and change it.
